## Links and compression strut
'<small>Source: NEN-EN 1992-1-1 6.2.2(6) (6.6N); 6.2.3 (6.7N), (6.8), (6.9), (6.18); 9.2.2 (9.4), (9.5N)</small>
'<i>The angle of the compression strut is a choice: a flatter strut gives the links more capacity and the concrete less. The chart shows that trade-off.</i>
V_Ed = 180 kN'<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
b_w = 300 mm'<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
d = 450 mm'<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
φ_w = 8 mm', link diameter<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
n_w = 2', legs per link<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
s_l = 200 mm', link spacing<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
f_ck = 30 N/mm^2'<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
f_yk = 500 N/mm^2'<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
α_cw = 1.0'<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
cot_θ = 2.5', between 1 and 2.5 (6.7N)<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
f_cd = f_ck/1.5
f_ywd = f_yk/1.15
A_sw = n_w*π*φ_w^2/4 to mm^2
z = 0.9*d to mm
ν_1 = 0.6*(1 - f_ck/(250 MPa))', (6.6N)'
V_s(c) = A_sw/s_l*z*f_ywd*c
V_max(c) = α_cw*b_w*z*ν_1*f_cd/(c + 1/c)
cot_θ,r = max(1; min(cot_θ; 2.5))', cot θ within the limits of (6.7N)'
#if cot_θ,r ≠ cot_θ
'cot θ is outside 1 to 2.5: the sheet uses the nearest limit.
#end if
V_Rd,s = V_s(cot_θ,r) to kN', (6.8)'
V_Rd,max = V_max(cot_θ,r) to kN', (6.9)'
UC_V = V_Ed/min(V_Rd,s; V_Rd,max)
s_l,max = min(0.75*d; 300 mm) to mm', 9.2.2(6) (NA)'
UC_sl = s_l/s_l,max
ρ_w = A_sw/(s_l*b_w)', (9.4)'
ρ_w,min = 0.08*sqrt(f_ck/MPa)/(f_yk/MPa)', (9.5N)'
UC_ρ = ρ_w,min/ρ_w
#if max(UC_sl; UC_ρ) > 1
'These links do not meet 9.2.2: too far apart or too few.
#end if
ΔF_td = 0.5*V_Ed*cot_θ,r to kN', (6.18), extra tensile force the longitudinal reinforcement must carry; check it separately'
#hide
PlotHeight = 220
#show
$Plot{V_s(x)/kN & V_max(x)/kN & V_Ed/kN @ x = 1 : 2.5}
'<span style="color:#D97706; font-weight:700;">━━ V<sub>Rd,s</sub></span> &nbsp; <span style="color:#2563EB; font-weight:700;">━━ V<sub>Rd,max</sub></span> &nbsp; <span style="color:#16A34A; font-weight:700;">━━ V<sub>Ed</sub></span> &nbsp; in kN, horizontal axis cot θ.
